// ============================================================================
//  mod_blundergat.zone  -  MOB OF THE DEAD'S BLUNDERGAT, ON EVERY MAP  (v2.17.32)
//
//  User, 2026-09-21: *"make sure that the blundergat is in the mystery box on
//  every mob of the dead survival map and any map that it can be added to"*,
//  then 2026-09-22: *"just the same way you've put weapons from other maps to
//  other maps just do the same thing."*  This is that same mechanism, thirteenth
//  gun in, and it follows mod_dragunov.zone line for line.
//
//  SOURCE: every asset below exists in zm_prison.ff, verified with
//  Unlinker --list before this file was written. build_ff.bat already --load's
//  zm_prison.ff (slot 5), so the Linker can resolve all of them with no new
//  --load and no raw art of our own.
//
//  The original port missed two assets named by the upgraded definition:
//  t6_wpn_zmb_blundergat_armor_view and _world. The reload animation exposes
//  the armor view attachment, so a missing model can fill the screen with
//  invalid geometry. Both forms now have every nonempty model reference here.
//
//  The Remington's camo_870mcs is also not a valid cross-map camo table for
//  this gun. Some maps own a shorter copy, and its slots 3 and 12 do not map
//  the Blundergat material. Both raw definitions use camo_qol_blundergat,
//  which the mod alone owns and fills for stock and animated PaP indices.
//
//  Other references read straight out of the def:
//      hudIcon/killIcon/   menu_mp_weapons_870mcs <- an MP asset; common_mp.ff
//      ammoCounterIcon                               and patch_mp.ff load on
//                                                    every zombies map
//      displayName         ZMWEAPON_BLUNDERGAT    <- en_patch_zm.ff, which every
//      (and _UPGRADED)                               map loads. Confirmed by
//                                                    dumping that zone's .str,
//                                                    not by hoping.
//  The materials and images come along as xmodel sub-assets.
//
//  🛑 THE WEAPON DEFS ARE NOT DECLARED HERE, same rule as every other ported
//  gun: the Linker never reads a raw weapon file, and a declared one would be
//  pulled from zm_prison.ff instead. They ship raw in weapons\zm\ -
//  blundergat_zm 19,985 B and blundergat_upgraded_zm 20,106 B, both under the
//  20,480 runtime-loader ceiling after the two standard trims (the 60
//  grenade-bounce coefficients and the 24 all-zero attachWorldModelOffset
//  fields; both were needed, trim 1 alone left them at 20,697 and 20,818).
//
//  📝 ON MOB THE RAW DEFS SHADOW THE MAP'S OWN, and that is intended and
//  harmless: they are that same def minus fields that are all zero on this
//  weapon. The trimmer is byte-exact - run over stock slowgun_upgraded_zm it
//  reproduces this mod's own shipped copy of that file apart from the one camo
//  key v2.11.0 deliberately changed.
//
//  The four muzzle flashes ARE declared below (2026-09-25). The first port left
//  them out on the theory that a def's fx string "resolves leniently", and it
//  does - to nothing. Every non-Mob boot logged
//      Could not load fx "weapon/blundersplat/fx_blundersplat_muzzleflash"
//  and the gun fired with no flash. The Unlinker cannot DUMP an FxEffectDef,
//  but the Linker copies one out of a --load'ed zone like any other asset;
//  mod_betty.zone and mod_bo1guns.zone already ship map-only fx this way.
//  zm_prison.ff is --load'ed, so these resolve with no raw .efx.
// ============================================================================

// View and world models. Both forms use the main pair; the upgraded form also
// uses the armor pair as attachment 6. The _acid models belong to Acid Gat.
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_blundergat_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_blundergat_world
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_blundergat_armor_view
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_blundergat_armor_world
camo,camo_qol_blundergat

// Muzzle flashes named by viewFlashEffect / worldFlashEffect; zm_prison.ff only.
fx,weapon/blundersplat/fx_blundersplat_muzzleflash
fx,weapon/blundersplat/fx_blundersplat_muzzleflash_3p
fx,weapon/blundersplat/fx_blundersplat_muzzleflash_ug
fx,weapon/blundersplat/fx_blundersplat_muzzleflash_ug_3p

